The autoleveling folder contains all the core functionality for automating in-game character progression, including configuration management, path execution, and data storage. It integrates with the game's movement and encounter systems to create autonomous leveling experiences while maintaining user preferences and saved targets. The folder serves as the central hub for parsing, executing, and persisting autoleveling workflows through its various specialized modules.

The runtime (autoleveling-engine.ts) drives a full leveling round — rest, buffs, movement, encounters, fight — and layers several composable gating mechanisms on top of the base script-action model: optional vitals gates (hp/mp/mv threshold), once-per-round/once-per-fight limits, round-boundary tracking (queue-buildup detection feeding both the `~` clear and an auto-tuned, persisted per-ability cooldown), an out-of-combat Rest cycle, and an out-of-combat Weight/carry-capacity gate. Config for all of this (AutoLevelConfig, v3) is authored through the wizard in `components/wizard/` and this folder's own read-through IndexedDB caches (areas, classes) plus the localStorage-backed per-connection config and IndexedDB-backed player overlay stores (targets/buffs/fight rows/prefs/learned cooldowns).
